      "readme_excerpt": "# 19 — Markovify (Text Generation / Prediction)\n\n**Library:** `markovify` v0.9.4 (3.4k GitHub stars)\n**Type:** Markov chain text generator — predicts next words from writing style\n**Use case:** Clipboard autocomplete, writing prediction, \"David would say...\"\n**Model size:** Proportional to training corpus — a few MB for large corpus\n**Status:** Installed, needs training corpus (clipboard history + vault text)\n\n## Connection to PPK\nMarkovify is a specialist — it only does text prediction.\nFeed it David's clipboard JSONL + Obsidian vault text -> it generates sentences in David's style.\nCould power: autocomplete in HTML editor, suggested clipboard items, writing drafts.\n\n## Training source candidates\n- D:\\BIL\\exports\\clipboard_history.jsonl (clipboard text)\n- O:\\_Theophysics_v4\\ (Obsidian vault markdown)\n- faiththruphysics.com articles (published writing)\n\n## Quick test\n```python\nimport markovify\ntext = open(\"corpus.txt\").read()\nmodel = markovify.Text(text)\nprint(model.make_sentence())\n```\n",
